{"id":"hin-t1-0001","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"price.bill","domain":3,"text_native":"बिल/चेक लाइये","text_romanized":"bil/cek lāiye","text_english":"The bill, please.","source_caption":"The check, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Where the word for bill and the word for receipt are the same word and neither is 'account'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0002","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"सस्ता","text_romanized":"sastā","text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0003","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"महंगा","text_romanized":"mehnga","text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"expensive","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0004","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"food.menu","domain":4,"text_native":"मेणयू कर्ड दीजिये","text_romanized":"menyoo kard diijiyeh","text_english":"The menu, please.","source_caption":"Can I look at the menu, please?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"One question covers a whole meal. Most phrasebooks waste slots on individual dishes instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0005","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"food.no-meat","domain":4,"text_native":"मैं सुअर का मांस नहीं खाता/-ती","text_romanized":"main suar ka māns nahīn khāta/-ī","text_english":"I do not eat meat.","source_caption":"I don't eat pork.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying it once at the start of the trip saves a refusal at the table, where it is awkward for both sides.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0006","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"पानी, जल","text_romanized":"pānī, jal","text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0007","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"सीधे","text_romanized":"sīdhe","text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"straight ahead","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0008","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"बायीं तरफ़ मुड़िये","text_romanized":"bāyīn muDiye","text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"Turn left.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0009","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"दाहिनी तरफ़ मुड़िये","text_romanized":"dāhinī muDiye","text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"Turn right.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0010","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"मुझे डॉक्टर चाहिये ।","text_romanized":"mujhe doctor chahie","text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0011","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"health.hurt","domain":9,"text_native":"मुझे चोट लगी है ।","text_romanized":"mujhe chot lagi hai","text_english":"I have been injured.","source_caption":"I've been injured.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Declares the situation before being asked. Several of these languages change tense or register on the word for injury, and the flat version sounds like a complaint.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0012","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"मुझे मत छूओ ।","text_romanized":"mujhe chunā mat/mujhe mat chuo","text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0013","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"यह एक मुसिबत है ।","text_romanized":"yeh ek musibat hai","text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0014","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"मैं रास्ता भूल गया ।","text_romanized":"main rasta bhul gaya","text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0015","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"क्या मै फ़ोन कर सकता हूं?","text_romanized":"kya main phone kar sakta hoon ?","text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0016","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"I'll call the police. पोलीस को बुलाता हूं ।","text_romanized":"main police ko bulaaoonga","text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"I'll call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"hin-t1-0017","lang":"hin","tier":1,"slot":"help.thief","domain":10,"text_native":"रुको! चोर!","text_romanized":"rukho! chor","text_english":"Stop, thief!","source_caption":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Loud, and aimed at a crowd rather than at one person. Included because the vocabulary exists and because it is the sentence that makes people nearby move.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Hindi phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Hindi_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
